// Timeline Demo: Time-Sensitive Quest
// Demonstrates @timeline, @time, and @schedule directives

=== start ===
@timeline start=480 scale=1 dayLength=1440

You wake up to your alarm blaring.

var quest_accepted = false
var met_deadline = false

* [Check the time] -> check_time
* [Get ready] -> get_ready

=== check_time ===
The clock reads 8:00 AM.

You remember - there's a meeting with the guild master at noon!

* [Better hurry!] -> get_ready

=== get_ready ===
@time advance=30

You shower, dress, and grab a quick breakfast.

Half an hour passes.

* [Head to the guild hall] -> guild_hall
* [Train for a bit first] -> morning_training

=== morning_training ===
@time advance=60

You spend an hour practicing your swordplay.

{$time.hour >= 12}
  Oh no! You're late for the meeting!
  -> late_arrival
{else}
  You feel more prepared now.
  -> guild_hall
{/}

=== guild_hall ===
You arrive at the guild hall.

{$time.hour < 12}
  You made it with time to spare!
  -> on_time_arrival
{else}
  The guild master looks annoyed at your tardiness.
  -> late_arrival
{/}

=== on_time_arrival ===
~ met_deadline = true

"Right on time!" the guild master greets you warmly.

"I have an urgent quest. A monster has been spotted in the nearby forest."

"It only appears at night. You'll need to wait for darkness."

~ quest_accepted = true

* [Accept the quest] -> wait_for_night

=== late_arrival ===
"You're late," the guild master says coldly.

"The quest has already been given to another adventurer."

Your reputation takes a hit.

-> failed_ending

=== wait_for_night ===
@schedule at=1200 goto=evening_arrives

You spend the afternoon preparing:
- Sharpening your sword
- Stocking up on potions
- Reviewing monster weaknesses

Time passes slowly as you wait for evening...

* [Rest until nightfall] -> rest

=== rest ===
@time advance=360

You rest for 6 hours.

-> evening_arrives

=== evening_arrives ===
{$time.period == "night"}
  The sun has set. Darkness falls over the town.

  It's time to hunt the monster!

  * [Enter the forest] -> night_forest
{else}
  The evening approaches. You prepare for the hunt.

  @time advance=120

  -> evening_arrives
{/}

=== night_forest ===
@scene bg="dark_forest.jpg" music="ominous.mp3"

You venture into the dark forest.

The moon casts eerie shadows between the trees.

{$time.hour >= 0 && $time.hour < 4}
  This is the witching hour - when monsters are most active!

  You hear a growl...

  * [Draw your weapon] -> monster_encounter
{else}
  It's still too early. You need to wait for deeper darkness.

  @time advance=60

  -> night_forest
{/}

=== monster_encounter ===
@audio play="monster_roar.mp3"
@image show="forest_monster.png"

A massive beast emerges from the shadows!

{met_deadline}
  Your morning training pays off - you feel confident!

  You fight bravely and slay the beast!

  -> victory_ending
{else}
  Without proper preparation, the fight is difficult.

  You barely manage to drive the beast away.

  -> partial_victory
{/}

=== victory_ending ===
@time advance=60

After an hour of intense combat, you emerge victorious!

You return to the guild hall at dawn with proof of your kill.

"Excellent work!" the guild master praises you.

Your reputation soars. Quest complete!

-> END

=== partial_victory ===
The beast flees, wounded but alive.

You return to the guild hall, exhausted.

"At least you survived," the guild master says.

"But the monster still lives. Someone else will have to finish it."

-> END

=== failed_ending ===
Sometimes timing is everything.

Maybe next time you'll be more punctual.

-> END
